Attribution
===========

ultraopen is an independent implementation, for opencode, of the workflow-orchestration and
effort-mode design introduced by Claude Code.

The tool description and the workflow-authoring reference adapt wording from Claude Code. That text
is kept close to the original deliberately: the model reads it at runtime and writes different code
as a result, so it is part of the implementation rather than documentation — paraphrasing it would
change what the tool does. Adaptations are limited to what opencode actually does, chiefly
`Workflow({...})` becoming `workflow({...})`, "the Agent tool" becoming "the task tool", and
`workflow_status` being a disk-only read of the run directory where the original tracks background
tasks in memory.
